1
00:00:14,097 --> 00:00:16,517
All right, everybody, settle down!

2
00:00:18,101 --> 00:00:19,060
Good.

3
00:00:19,144 --> 00:00:21,194
Now, Robby has something important to say.

4
00:00:21,271 --> 00:00:22,671
I know that this isn't easy.

5
00:00:22,731 --> 00:00:24,732
We're going to help you
address any challenges

6
00:00:24,816 --> 00:00:26,234
that you might be having.

7
00:00:26,318 --> 00:00:28,111
If you have any concerns,
just raise your hand.

8
00:00:28,195 --> 00:00:30,864
- Emma, write all this down.
- Dr. Mohan.

9
00:00:30,948 --> 00:00:33,116
Medication orders aren't coming up
from the pharmacy.

10
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:36,453
Check with the clinical pharmacist
to see if it's in the PDS.

11
00:00:36,537 --> 00:00:40,165
If it's not, then give the third copy
of the order sheet to Dr. Nordt.

12
00:00:40,249 --> 00:00:41,916
We're gonna need more people to run it down.

13
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,627
- We'll work on it. Langdon.
- I can't find the patient clipboards.

14
00:00:44,711 --> 00:00:47,111
Clipboards need to stay here
for orders and labs.

15
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:48,465
Wait, so how do we write our notes?

16
00:00:48,549 --> 00:00:51,468
Take the T sheet to the bedside,
not the whole chart.

17
00:00:51,552 --> 00:00:53,303
Same goes for nursing notes.

18
00:00:53,387 --> 00:00:55,096
- Princess.
- Fax machine is down.

19
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:57,474
- Error message E6.
- What the hell does that mean?

20
00:00:57,558 --> 00:00:59,808
- You can check the manual.
- There isn't one.

21
00:00:59,810 --> 00:01:01,686
Okay, Perlah, why don't you take
your phone out to the base?

22
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:04,170
See if you can get service,
find a manual online.

23
00:01:08,151 --> 00:01:09,694
What else? Ogilvie, put your hand down.

24
00:01:09,778 --> 00:01:12,030
- Santos.
- We've gotten a few CT results back

25
00:01:12,114 --> 00:01:13,464
but nothing on plain films.

26
00:01:13,532 --> 00:01:15,116
That's probably because they're all sitting

27
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:17,285
on the portable machine
not getting to radiology.

28
00:01:17,369 --> 00:01:18,995
- I'll take care of this.
- You be patient.

29
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:20,998
Help each other. Thank you.

30
00:01:21,999 --> 00:01:23,583
We need to call in extra help.

31
00:01:23,667 --> 00:01:26,419
At 3:00 p.m. on a holiday?
I know people, buddy.

32
00:01:26,503 --> 00:01:29,422
I have a 32-year-old woman
with severe abdominal pain.

33
00:01:29,506 --> 00:01:31,132
- Do we have a bed?
- Not at the moment.

34
00:01:31,216 --> 00:01:32,300
- I'll take her.
- Incoming.

35
00:01:32,384 --> 00:01:33,468
Thank you.

36
00:01:33,552 --> 00:01:35,178
Santos, Javadi, you're up.

37
00:01:35,262 --> 00:01:36,722
Trauma one's open.

38
00:01:37,848 --> 00:01:39,265
12-year-old Jude Augustin--

39
00:01:39,349 --> 00:01:41,935
Firecracker exploded, nondominant left hand.

40
00:01:42,019 --> 00:01:43,895
Good vitals. 25 of fent so far.

41
00:01:43,979 --> 00:01:44,812
Any other injuries?

42
00:01:44,896 --> 00:01:46,648
No, but seems to have
lost two of his fingers.

43
00:01:46,732 --> 00:01:48,191
- Did you bring 'em?
- Blown to bits.

44
00:01:48,275 --> 00:01:50,026
- It really hurts.
- I'm sure it does.

45
00:01:50,110 --> 00:01:51,861
We'll do something for that.

46
00:01:51,945 --> 00:01:53,655
- Parents?
- Not on scene.

47
00:01:56,158 --> 00:01:57,075
Ready?

48
00:01:57,159 --> 00:01:59,035
One, two, three.

49
00:01:59,119 --> 00:02:02,664
Hey, Jude, do you know your mom
or your dad's telephone number?

50
00:02:02,748 --> 00:02:05,083
No. But I know my sister's.

51
00:02:05,167 --> 00:02:06,168
Okay.

52
00:02:06,877 --> 00:02:09,254
- Good breath sounds.
- Abdomen nontender.

53
00:02:09,338 --> 00:02:10,630
Heart rate 112.

54
00:02:10,714 --> 00:02:12,006
Put this around his left forearm.

55
00:02:12,090 --> 00:02:13,341
- Is that good?
- That is very good.

56
00:02:13,425 --> 00:02:16,678
I want to do another 25 of fent
before we open this bandage.

57
00:02:16,762 --> 00:02:18,429
Can you tell us what happened?

58
00:02:18,513 --> 00:02:21,307
- My friends had firecrackers.
- 25 fent on board.

59
00:02:21,391 --> 00:02:24,018
I lit one, and it went off fast.

60
00:02:24,102 --> 00:02:26,104
I-I dropped it, but...

61
00:02:26,188 --> 00:02:27,939
We're gonna take your bandage off now, okay?

62
00:02:28,023 --> 00:02:29,816
- I don't want to see.
- You don't have to.

63
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:31,609
Just look at me.

64
00:02:31,693 --> 00:02:32,986
Okay.

65
00:02:33,070 --> 00:02:34,071
Cutting.

66
00:02:36,865 --> 00:02:38,157
Sorry.

67
00:02:38,241 --> 00:02:39,660
You're doing great.

68
00:02:42,496 --> 00:02:45,123
That looks like a lot more
than a firecracker.

69
00:02:45,207 --> 00:02:48,876
- More like an M-80 or a cherry bomb.
- It's really good that you dropped it.

70
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:50,510
You saved the rest of your hand.

71
00:02:50,545 --> 00:02:52,171
Digits four and five avulsed.

72
00:02:52,255 --> 00:02:55,466
Distal metacarpals four and five
also gone with exposed bone.

73
00:02:55,550 --> 00:02:58,177
Soft-tissue damage on the palmar aspect,
less so on dorsal--

74
00:02:58,261 --> 00:02:59,679
Some burns on wound edges.

75
00:02:59,763 --> 00:03:02,263
Jude, can you bend your fingers
for me up and down?

76
00:03:04,017 --> 00:03:05,852
Really good job. Really good job.

77
00:03:05,936 --> 00:03:08,605
- How bad is it?
- You lost two fingers.

78
00:03:08,689 --> 00:03:10,898
But it seems like the rest are gonna be okay.

79
00:03:10,982 --> 00:03:13,318
Oh, no. I fucked up!

80
00:03:14,111 --> 00:03:15,862
All right, can we do
a wrist block for the pain?

81
00:03:15,946 --> 00:03:18,656
I want to do a very detailed
motor and sensory exam first.

82
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:21,284
We're gonna continue
our exam now, okay, Jude?

83
00:03:24,538 --> 00:03:25,913
Okay, thanks.

84
00:03:25,997 --> 00:03:28,249
ICU can take her after the next neuro exam.

85
00:03:28,333 --> 00:03:29,667
The ICU?

86
00:03:29,751 --> 00:03:32,601
It's just so she can be monitored
for the rest of the day.

87
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:35,257
Four millimeters and reactive.

88
00:03:36,925 --> 00:03:38,092
Mel.

89
00:03:38,176 --> 00:03:40,762
- Four millimeters and reactive.
- Yep, got it.

90
00:03:40,846 --> 00:03:42,639
I could sort of make out your hand.

91
00:03:46,768 --> 00:03:48,770
Can you cover your good eye?

92
00:03:48,854 --> 00:03:50,939
How many fingers am I holding up?

93
00:03:52,232 --> 00:03:53,191
Three.

94
00:03:55,318 --> 00:03:56,694
That's good news.

95
00:03:56,778 --> 00:03:59,947
So the medicine worked?
She's out of the woods?

96
00:04:00,031 --> 00:04:01,240
Possibly.

97
00:04:01,324 --> 00:04:02,367
It's...

98
00:04:02,451 --> 00:04:04,327
Okay, cover your eye again.

99
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:07,539
All right, what do you see?

100
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:12,169
- Top line is E.
- All right, and the next one?

101
00:04:14,713 --> 00:04:15,839
Nothing.

102
00:04:16,715 --> 00:04:18,467
Okay, well, that's 20/200.

103
00:04:19,968 --> 00:04:21,469
Meaning?

104
00:04:21,553 --> 00:04:24,653
What a healthy eye can see at 200 feet,
she can see at 20 feet.

105
00:04:24,723 --> 00:04:27,600
- Is that good?
- Yeah. It's much better.

106
00:04:27,684 --> 00:04:30,353
And it can continue to improve over time.

107
00:04:31,563 --> 00:04:32,773
Thank you, Dr. King.

108
00:04:34,775 --> 00:04:37,485
I'm gonna take a quick break
before my deposition.

109
00:04:37,569 --> 00:04:40,905
So I'll let Robby know
that I'm off the clock for the time being.

110
00:04:40,989 --> 00:04:42,783
- Good luck.
- Thanks.

111
00:04:45,994 --> 00:04:47,495
- Mel.
- Hey.

112
00:04:47,579 --> 00:04:48,871
You have a visitor in chairs.

113
00:04:48,955 --> 00:04:52,041
- What? Who?
- Said she's your sister.

114
00:04:52,125 --> 00:04:53,210
Becca?

115
00:04:57,506 --> 00:04:59,298
Yep. You have heat exhaustion.

116
00:04:59,382 --> 00:05:03,136
It usually gets better with Aleve,
but today was really bad.

117
00:05:03,220 --> 00:05:04,513
Same pain you had before?

118
00:05:05,472 --> 00:05:07,724
- From a cyst?
- I think so.

119
00:05:07,808 --> 00:05:09,767
I have PCOS.

120
00:05:09,851 --> 00:05:12,437
Is the pain always on your left?

121
00:05:12,521 --> 00:05:13,813
Today it is.

122
00:05:13,897 --> 00:05:16,733
We will check a UA and urine pregnancy test,

123
00:05:16,817 --> 00:05:18,317
and I'll give you a shot of Toradol.

124
00:05:18,401 --> 00:05:20,862
It's something a little stronger
for the pain.

125
00:05:20,946 --> 00:05:22,655
I'm not pregnant, I promise.

126
00:05:22,739 --> 00:05:25,950
No, we have to. It's hospital policy.

127
00:05:26,034 --> 00:05:28,537
You guys still write stuff down on paper?

128
00:05:29,538 --> 00:05:31,623
Today we do, yeah.

129
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:42,341
Are you a doctor?
I've been waiting hours to be seen.

130
00:05:42,425 --> 00:05:43,551
Quick question--

131
00:05:43,635 --> 00:05:46,429
- Hey, watch the walker.
- This thing is useless.

132
00:05:47,264 --> 00:05:48,973
Sorry, I just...

133
00:05:49,057 --> 00:05:51,852
We're really busy,
and someone will see you in a second.

134
00:05:54,187 --> 00:05:56,273
- Becca.
- Mel, hi.

135
00:05:57,274 --> 00:06:00,026
- Is everything okay?
- Yeah, I have a stomachache.

136
00:06:00,110 --> 00:06:01,903
Did you see the residential-care nurse?

137
00:06:01,987 --> 00:06:04,447
She was out for the Fourth,
but I talked to her on the phone.

138
00:06:04,531 --> 00:06:06,866
She told me to come here,
and Geri brought me.

139
00:06:06,950 --> 00:06:08,284
- Thank you.
- No problem.

140
00:06:08,368 --> 00:06:10,453
- I'll wait for you.
- Okay.

141
00:06:10,537 --> 00:06:11,872
Okay. Come on, this way.

142
00:06:12,873 --> 00:06:14,123
Just through here.

143
00:06:14,207 --> 00:06:18,002
- Is it always like this?
- Yeah, pretty much.

144
00:06:18,086 --> 00:06:21,255
Wow. There are a lot of smelly people.

145
00:06:21,339 --> 00:06:22,632
Yeah.

146
00:06:22,716 --> 00:06:24,008
Are you going to help them all?

147
00:06:24,092 --> 00:06:26,219
Yeah, but let's start with you first.

148
00:06:26,303 --> 00:06:27,304
Okay.

149
00:06:28,179 --> 00:06:31,808
- How's the pain?
- I can't feel my hand anymore.

150
00:06:31,892 --> 00:06:33,017
Ancef's on board.

151
00:06:33,101 --> 00:06:36,301
Okay, we're going to clean
out your hand with saline--salt water.

152
00:06:36,313 --> 00:06:37,689
Okay.

153
00:06:41,484 --> 00:06:42,402
What's up?

154
00:06:43,111 --> 00:06:46,739
- Hand versus M-80.
- Surprised we've only seen one of these.

155
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:48,199
The day's still young yet.

156
00:06:48,283 --> 00:06:50,409
Lost fourth metacarpal,
mid-shaft on the fifth.

157
00:06:50,493 --> 00:06:51,494
Bummer.

158
00:06:52,871 --> 00:06:55,081
Hello, I'm Dr. Garcia from surgery.

159
00:06:55,165 --> 00:06:56,749
- I'm gonna have surgery?
- Yes.

160
00:06:56,833 --> 00:06:59,418
The first operation is to clean everything up

161
00:06:59,502 --> 00:07:01,302
and cover where the skin is missing.

162
00:07:02,005 --> 00:07:05,055
But you still have your thumb
and your most important fingers.

163
00:07:09,262 --> 00:07:11,931
- What'd you give him for pain?
- We did regional blocks.

164
00:07:12,015 --> 00:07:14,684
Hand surgery always wants to document
their own neuro exam.

165
00:07:14,768 --> 00:07:16,978
Sensation is intact
to light touch and pinprick

166
00:07:17,062 --> 00:07:19,212
throughout the digits in the remaining hand.

167
00:07:21,524 --> 00:07:25,695
Yeah, FDS and FTPs and extensor function
was all intact.

168
00:07:25,779 --> 00:07:28,406
- Need parental consent for surgery.
- Yeah, we're working on that.

169
00:07:28,490 --> 00:07:29,532
Dr. Robby?

170
00:07:33,870 --> 00:07:35,747
I smell alcohol on his breath.

171
00:07:37,207 --> 00:07:39,792
He's in line for the OR.
Might be a little bit of a wait.

172
00:07:39,876 --> 00:07:41,085
Ortho's still in with Allen Billings--

173
00:07:41,169 --> 00:07:43,045
That open shoulder dislocation
that came back from Westbridge.

174
00:07:43,129 --> 00:07:44,297
He's still in surgery?

175
00:07:44,381 --> 00:07:46,299
He waited an hour
to be cleared by anesthesia.

176
00:07:46,383 --> 00:07:48,384
Is the insurance company
gonna cover the cost of the surgery?

177
00:07:48,468 --> 00:07:49,886
Yeah, since Westbridge is still down.

178
00:07:49,970 --> 00:07:51,220
Well, good, because the delay in care

179
00:07:51,304 --> 00:07:53,389
definitely increased the chance
of a post-op infection.

180
00:07:53,473 --> 00:07:56,773
You got to love it when insurance
companies make medical decisions.

181
00:07:57,978 --> 00:07:59,520
- Hey.
- What's up?

182
00:07:59,604 --> 00:08:02,654
Do you still need a rain check
for watching fireworks tonight?

183
00:08:02,691 --> 00:08:04,241
I thought you were coming over.

184
00:08:04,275 --> 00:08:05,568
I made other plans.

185
00:08:06,987 --> 00:08:08,404
Okay, cool.

186
00:08:08,488 --> 00:08:10,489
I'll try hitting you up tomorrow.

187
00:08:10,573 --> 00:08:12,575
We're just keeping it casual, right?

188
00:08:12,659 --> 00:08:13,785
For sure.

189
00:08:17,998 --> 00:08:20,791
Yeah. Thank you.
Yeah, bye.

190
00:08:20,875 --> 00:08:21,918
Oh, hey.

191
00:08:22,002 --> 00:08:23,711
I just got a hold of the sister
of the heavy patient

192
00:08:23,795 --> 00:08:25,338
Abbot's taking to Presby.

193
00:08:25,422 --> 00:08:26,797
She still lives in Arizona,

194
00:08:26,881 --> 00:08:29,717
but she is willing to talk
to him when he's back.

195
00:08:29,801 --> 00:08:30,801
That's good news.

196
00:08:30,885 --> 00:08:32,720
When do you think that might be?

197
00:08:32,804 --> 00:08:35,014
Depends on how crazy it is over at Presby.

198
00:08:35,098 --> 00:08:36,849
If it's anything like here, who knows?

199
00:08:36,933 --> 00:08:37,934
Yeah.

200
00:08:38,810 --> 00:08:41,228
- Is help on the way?
- Ah, ye of little faith.

201
00:08:41,312 --> 00:08:42,814
You got a gumband?

202
00:08:44,024 --> 00:08:46,234
Thanks. Keep losing these.

203
00:08:47,193 --> 00:08:48,945
Oh, this fucking day.

204
00:08:49,029 --> 00:08:51,447
Thought I was gonna get
a clean getaway for my trip.

205
00:08:51,531 --> 00:08:54,742
God gives His toughest battles
to His strongest soldiers.

206
00:08:54,826 --> 00:08:57,076
Dana, is there a room open?
This is my sister.

207
00:08:57,078 --> 00:08:59,205
She's in a lot of pain,
and we need a bed ASAP.

208
00:08:59,289 --> 00:09:00,989
My name is Becca, not "my sister."

209
00:09:01,041 --> 00:09:02,166
Sorry, right.

210
00:09:02,250 --> 00:09:05,711
- Dana, Dr. Robby, this is my--
- Becca.

211
00:09:05,795 --> 00:09:07,004
Nice to meet you.

212
00:09:07,088 --> 00:09:10,049
You're Dr. Robby? Cool.

213
00:09:10,133 --> 00:09:12,593
Central seven was just cleaned.
Anything I can get you, hon?

214
00:09:12,677 --> 00:09:14,054
No, thank you.

215
00:09:17,265 --> 00:09:18,850
Oh, wait, Becca. Come here.

216
00:09:19,851 --> 00:09:22,854
Come this way.
We're going right in here.

217
00:09:24,064 --> 00:09:27,024
All right, so you're gonna
need to get undressed

218
00:09:27,108 --> 00:09:29,652
and get into the gown,
which should be on the bed.

219
00:09:29,736 --> 00:09:32,363
Then we're gonna do an evaluation
and take a history.

220
00:09:32,447 --> 00:09:33,864
That's a lot of questions,

221
00:09:33,948 --> 00:09:35,908
like, like, a lot, a lot of questions,
which we'll do.

222
00:09:35,992 --> 00:09:37,660
And then a physical exam, of course.

223
00:09:37,744 --> 00:09:39,996
Mel, I've been to the doctor's before.

224
00:09:41,289 --> 00:09:42,581
Right. Sorry.

225
00:09:42,665 --> 00:09:45,668
- I just--
- I really want this to be done the right way.

226
00:09:49,714 --> 00:09:51,465
Do you need to take that call?

227
00:09:51,549 --> 00:09:53,843
No, it's a reminder alarm

228
00:09:53,927 --> 00:09:56,804
for this important meeting
I have in 15 minutes.

229
00:09:56,888 --> 00:09:57,972
Do you have to go?

230
00:09:59,099 --> 00:10:01,017
Let's just get you
taken care of first, all right?

231
00:10:01,101 --> 00:10:03,519
So just change into the gown.
I'll be behind the curtain.

232
00:10:03,603 --> 00:10:04,604
Okay.

233
00:10:06,147 --> 00:10:07,148
Okay.

234
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:19,953
Your grand prize.

235
00:10:20,912 --> 00:10:23,915
All I see is green, baby.

236
00:10:32,924 --> 00:10:34,633
What's up with her?

237
00:10:34,717 --> 00:10:36,761
Fax machine has paper jam, so annoying.

238
00:10:45,436 --> 00:10:47,646
- You want me to try?
- No.

239
00:10:47,730 --> 00:10:50,066
- Oh, huzzah.
- I got it.

240
00:10:54,404 --> 00:10:55,905
- What's it say?
- "Replace toner."

241
00:10:55,989 --> 00:10:57,073
We live in hell.

242
00:10:57,157 --> 00:10:59,116
- Oh, where can we get that?
- 1988.

243
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:01,660
- You ever seen one of these?
- Honestly, no.

244
00:11:01,744 --> 00:11:03,662
How are we gonna get labs
and X-rays to the wards?

245
00:11:03,746 --> 00:11:05,664
The old-fashioned way, runners.

246
00:11:05,748 --> 00:11:08,648
I'll check if they can spare
a couple clerks from upstairs.

247
00:11:13,256 --> 00:11:16,092
When were you first diagnosed
with polycystic ovarian syndrome?

248
00:11:16,176 --> 00:11:17,301
Last summer.

249
00:11:17,385 --> 00:11:19,095
That's when the symptoms started?

250
00:11:19,179 --> 00:11:22,056
No. I've had years of pain, hormonal changes,

251
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:23,516
and an abnormal period.

252
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:27,645
I was finally diagnosed after switching
to a gyno who actually listened to me.

253
00:11:27,729 --> 00:11:30,023
Yeah, it can take time to make the diagnosis.

254
00:11:31,149 --> 00:11:33,693
That sounds like an excuse
for lazy doctoring.

255
00:11:34,611 --> 00:11:37,279
And it doesn't help that some
of you don't listen to women,

256
00:11:37,363 --> 00:11:39,115
let alone brown ones.

257
00:11:39,199 --> 00:11:40,658
It hasn't been easy.

258
00:11:40,742 --> 00:11:42,827
- How's your pain now?
- Better.

259
00:11:42,911 --> 00:11:45,204
- What was she given?
- IM Toradol.

260
00:11:45,288 --> 00:11:48,374
Have you had
a transvaginal ultrasound before?

261
00:11:48,458 --> 00:11:50,209
I've lost count of how many times.

262
00:11:50,293 --> 00:11:52,545
Okay, if you want to scoot your bottom down,

263
00:11:52,629 --> 00:11:55,548
I'll help you put your feet
in the leg rests here.

264
00:11:55,632 --> 00:11:57,800
Yep, you got it.

265
00:12:06,309 --> 00:12:08,227
Okay, ready to go here?

266
00:12:08,311 --> 00:12:11,022
Cold gel and some pressure.

267
00:12:13,983 --> 00:12:14,984
Okay.

268
00:12:16,361 --> 00:12:21,240
Okay, ectopic is unlikely
since the urine pregnancy was negative.

269
00:12:21,324 --> 00:12:22,950
I'm hoping it'll be positive one day.

270
00:12:23,034 --> 00:12:25,494
- Oh, are you trying?
- Not at the moment.

271
00:12:25,578 --> 00:12:27,663
I'm getting married in September.

272
00:12:27,747 --> 00:12:29,666
- Oh, congratulations.
- Okay.

273
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:34,044
A bunch of small cysts--to be expected.

274
00:12:34,128 --> 00:12:37,381
But then there's one big one,
about five centimeters.

275
00:12:37,465 --> 00:12:39,842
My gyno's been monitoring her.

276
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:42,386
With a little bit of free fluid.

277
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:45,014
Checking blood flow to the ovary.

278
00:12:45,098 --> 00:12:47,349
Red is for artery. Blue is for vein.

279
00:12:47,433 --> 00:12:49,185
Okay, looks good.

280
00:12:49,269 --> 00:12:50,687
Coming out now.

281
00:12:52,063 --> 00:12:53,064
- Sorry.
- Okay.

282
00:12:55,066 --> 00:12:58,486
We will be back when we get
your blood-test results.

283
00:13:01,239 --> 00:13:02,531
All right, what do you think?

284
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:05,618
She probably had a small fluid leak
from the cyst that caused the pain

285
00:13:05,702 --> 00:13:08,245
that improved with a nonsteroidal.

286
00:13:08,329 --> 00:13:11,498
- And what's your plan?
- Discharge with naproxen?

287
00:13:11,582 --> 00:13:15,628
Do you think that just might be
what her doctors in the past have done?

288
00:13:15,712 --> 00:13:18,631
Well, she said she's feeling better.
We can free up a bed.

289
00:13:18,715 --> 00:13:20,007
She didn't look good in triage,

290
00:13:20,091 --> 00:13:22,843
and her pain was way more severe
than previous episodes.

291
00:13:22,927 --> 00:13:24,845
I think we observe her for a bit.

292
00:13:24,929 --> 00:13:26,430
Okay.

293
00:13:26,514 --> 00:13:29,517
Mr. Green, this is Dr. Mohan
and student doctor Ogilvie.

294
00:13:30,727 --> 00:13:32,436
What can you tell me about your flank pain?

295
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:35,648
- Feels like another kidney stone.
- You've had them before?

296
00:13:35,732 --> 00:13:37,816
I said "another," which means
an additional thing

297
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:39,235
of the same type.

298
00:13:40,528 --> 00:13:42,280
I teach English at Point Park.

299
00:13:42,905 --> 00:13:44,114
Triggering.

300
00:13:44,198 --> 00:13:46,148
My dad's a high-school English teacher.

301
00:13:47,744 --> 00:13:50,394
Well, you went into medicine.
He must be really proud.

302
00:13:51,539 --> 00:13:53,207
You'd have to ask him.

303
00:13:53,291 --> 00:13:54,875
Getting back to your pain,

304
00:13:54,959 --> 00:13:57,253
it feels like something
you've experienced before?

305
00:13:57,337 --> 00:13:59,255
Same as always, left kidney.

306
00:13:59,339 --> 00:14:01,298
Started about 10:00 p.m. last night.

307
00:14:01,382 --> 00:14:02,883
Any fever, blood in the urine?

308
00:14:02,967 --> 00:14:04,760
No.
No fever.

309
00:14:04,844 --> 00:14:06,845
Urine's a bit darker than normal.

310
00:14:06,929 --> 00:14:08,806
Dehydration can lead to stone formation.

311
00:14:08,890 --> 00:14:10,391
Lean forward a bit, please.

312
00:14:10,475 --> 00:14:12,476
- Check for CVA tenderness.
- Yeah.

313
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:13,561
All right.

314
00:14:14,937 --> 00:14:17,148
Let me know if there's any discomfort.

315
00:14:20,109 --> 00:14:21,277
- Sorry.
- Yeah.

316
00:14:21,361 --> 00:14:23,761
- We'll order medication and a few tests.
- Okay.

317
00:14:28,368 --> 00:14:31,368
Dip urine, Chem Seven,
bedside ultrasound to check for hydro,

318
00:14:31,371 --> 00:14:32,705
and ketorolac for pain.

319
00:14:32,789 --> 00:14:34,374
- Sounds good.
- Okay.

320
00:14:39,962 --> 00:14:41,422
Really putting me to work.

321
00:14:41,506 --> 00:14:43,299
It's been a very busy day, Dr. Barker.

322
00:14:43,383 --> 00:14:44,384
Call me Nick.

323
00:14:46,969 --> 00:14:49,596
- What's all this?
- I brought radiology to us.

324
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:52,224
Dr. Barker, Nick, will have
wet-read results for us

325
00:14:52,308 --> 00:14:53,600
- in no time.
- Good idea.

326
00:14:53,684 --> 00:14:55,894
- Thank you.
- "Wet read"?

327
00:14:55,978 --> 00:14:58,981
- You ever take a photography class?
- Yeah, in, like, middle school.

328
00:14:59,065 --> 00:15:01,317
So, before digital technology, X-ray films

329
00:15:01,401 --> 00:15:04,737
were physically developed
in a darkroom, in baths, thus wet read.

330
00:15:04,821 --> 00:15:06,488
Oh, cool.

331
00:15:06,572 --> 00:15:08,408
He's taking up a lot of space.

332
00:15:09,367 --> 00:15:11,744
Got an update from Dylan
on our abandoned baby.

333
00:15:11,828 --> 00:15:14,663
CYF has requested an emergency
custody authorization.

334
00:15:14,747 --> 00:15:17,374
Once we get a court order,
we can place her in foster care.

335
00:15:17,458 --> 00:15:19,210
I love photography.

336
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:21,045
- Jesus Christ.
- Dr. Robby?

337
00:15:21,129 --> 00:15:22,546
Dr. Robby, can I borrow you for a second?

338
00:15:22,630 --> 00:15:23,756
Sure. What can I do for you?

339
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:25,132
Well, she said she has a stomachache,

340
00:15:25,216 --> 00:15:26,759
but belly pain can mean a lot
of different things--

341
00:15:26,843 --> 00:15:30,471
- Okay, okay, okay, breathe.
- I'm looking for Dr. Mel King.

342
00:15:30,555 --> 00:15:31,472
Yes?

343
00:15:32,557 --> 00:15:34,933
I'm Morgan Stiles,
one of the hospital's attorneys.

344
00:15:35,017 --> 00:15:37,567
I'm here to escort you upstairs
for your deposition.

345
00:15:37,645 --> 00:15:39,188
Right now?

346
00:15:39,272 --> 00:15:42,858
Morgan, can I borrow Dr. King
for just a moment?

347
00:15:42,942 --> 00:15:44,235
Sure.

348
00:15:46,028 --> 00:15:47,321
It's gonna be fine.

349
00:15:47,405 --> 00:15:49,406
I can't go up now because of Becca.

350
00:15:49,490 --> 00:15:51,590
You probably shouldn't be caring for Becca.

351
00:15:51,659 --> 00:15:53,452
It's not a good idea
to care for family members.

352
00:15:53,536 --> 00:15:54,936
It's hard to stay objective.

353
00:15:54,954 --> 00:15:56,372
Let's see who's available.

354
00:15:56,456 --> 00:15:57,706
Hey, are you free?

355
00:15:57,790 --> 00:15:59,500
Is anybody really free?

356
00:16:00,501 --> 00:16:01,586
Not an R2.

357
00:16:02,962 --> 00:16:04,463
Just the guy we were looking for.

358
00:16:04,547 --> 00:16:06,048
- Need something?
- Yes.

359
00:16:07,049 --> 00:16:07,966
Sure.

360
00:16:08,050 --> 00:16:11,053
Dr. King's sister has a bellyache.
The case is now yours.

361
00:16:11,137 --> 00:16:12,054
Sure.

362
00:16:12,138 --> 00:16:14,390
You can pick up the rest of her patients
while she's doing her deposition.

363
00:16:14,474 --> 00:16:16,392
How am I supposed to catch up
on my outstanding charts

364
00:16:16,476 --> 00:16:18,394
with extra patients
and the computer system down?

365
00:16:18,478 --> 00:16:19,978
The same way that the rest of us do.

366
00:16:20,062 --> 00:16:22,812
You can finish your charting
when you finish your shift.

367
00:16:22,815 --> 00:16:24,650
Fucking fantastic.

368
00:16:29,280 --> 00:16:31,198
- Hi, Becca.
- Hi.

369
00:16:31,282 --> 00:16:33,682
This is Dr. Langdon.
He'll be taking care of you.

370
00:16:33,701 --> 00:16:37,621
You have really nice hair, Dr. Langdon.

371
00:16:37,705 --> 00:16:39,206
Thank you.

372
00:16:39,290 --> 00:16:42,584
Mel, would you mind turning off
the lights on your way out?

373
00:16:42,668 --> 00:16:43,669
Of course.

374
00:16:44,504 --> 00:16:46,964
And I'll be back as soon as I'm done.

375
00:16:47,048 --> 00:16:49,049
And feel free to call me
if anything comes up,

376
00:16:49,133 --> 00:16:50,843
- because I can come right--
- Don't worry.

377
00:16:50,927 --> 00:16:53,304
- Becca's in good hands.
- I know.

378
00:16:54,305 --> 00:16:55,431
Okay.

379
00:17:03,105 --> 00:17:06,108
Mel says lots of nice things about you.

380
00:17:08,236 --> 00:17:09,237
Okay.

381
00:17:11,197 --> 00:17:13,365
Tell me the reason you're here today.

382
00:17:13,449 --> 00:17:14,783
I have a stomachache.

383
00:17:14,867 --> 00:17:16,660
Your belly hurts? Where about?

384
00:17:16,744 --> 00:17:19,746
- Right down here.
- Okay.

385
00:17:19,830 --> 00:17:23,584
Are you experiencing anything else,
or is it just the stomachache?

386
00:17:23,668 --> 00:17:25,627
It stings when I pee.

387
00:17:25,711 --> 00:17:27,671
Sometimes when that happens,

388
00:17:27,755 --> 00:17:30,382
women feel like they need
to urinate all the time.

389
00:17:30,466 --> 00:17:32,176
- Do you feel that way?
- Yes.

390
00:17:32,260 --> 00:17:33,969
And what happens when you go?

391
00:17:34,053 --> 00:17:36,097
Hardly anything comes out.

392
00:17:36,764 --> 00:17:38,182
That's what I thought.

393
00:17:38,266 --> 00:17:40,726
Really? How do you know?

394
00:17:40,810 --> 00:17:43,687
Well, I've seen a lot of patients
with the same symptoms.

395
00:17:43,771 --> 00:17:46,440
- So this is normal?
- Yes, it's totally normal.

396
00:17:46,524 --> 00:17:48,817
But we still need to fix it.

397
00:17:48,901 --> 00:17:49,986
Okay.

398
00:17:56,158 --> 00:17:57,284
Hey.

399
00:17:57,368 --> 00:17:58,995
How's it going, Roxy?

400
00:17:59,620 --> 00:18:01,788
- A little better.
- Yeah?

401
00:18:01,872 --> 00:18:03,624
You need more morphine?

402
00:18:09,589 --> 00:18:12,425
I've been in pain all this time, my love.

403
00:18:13,134 --> 00:18:15,011
Why didn't you tell me?

404
00:18:16,178 --> 00:18:18,180
I didn't want you guys to worry.

405
00:18:20,141 --> 00:18:21,934
I can't pretend anymore.

406
00:18:23,603 --> 00:18:26,856
Mom, it's so hot outside,
the ice cream's melting.

407
00:18:29,817 --> 00:18:32,028
We thought we'd indulge a bit.

408
00:18:32,987 --> 00:18:34,405
Oh, yeah.

409
00:18:35,406 --> 00:18:36,282
Looks amazing.

410
00:18:36,365 --> 00:18:38,825
So which flavor should we start with?

411
00:18:38,909 --> 00:18:41,037
Salty caramel, Mom's favorite.

412
00:18:42,038 --> 00:18:44,206
You'll need lots more napkins.

413
00:18:59,972 --> 00:19:00,890
Rude.

414
00:19:03,517 --> 00:19:06,770
- How's it going in there?
- All good. Langdon's great with her.

415
00:19:06,854 --> 00:19:08,564
I got seven more films ordered,
waiting to be shot,

416
00:19:08,648 --> 00:19:10,698
but Dr. Nick here's tying up the machine.

417
00:19:11,859 --> 00:19:14,194
Isn't there a USB port
on the front of that portable?

418
00:19:14,278 --> 00:19:16,947
And can't we just download
the films to a workstation

419
00:19:17,031 --> 00:19:18,657
and watch them without the Internet?

420
00:19:18,741 --> 00:19:20,993
- Yes.
- Oh, right. Forgot about that.

421
00:19:21,077 --> 00:19:23,370
Is he actually helping,
or is he just distracting?

422
00:19:23,454 --> 00:19:25,372
Let's download these
and start moving on to folks

423
00:19:25,456 --> 00:19:27,374
- waiting for X-rays.
- Great. I'm caught up anyway.

424
00:19:27,458 --> 00:19:29,001
I'll be back when the next batch is ready.

425
00:19:29,085 --> 00:19:31,211
Dr. Robby, the guardian
of your missing-fingers kid

426
00:19:31,295 --> 00:19:33,380
- in Central 12 has arrived.
- Thank you, Olive.

427
00:19:33,464 --> 00:19:35,340
Will you ask Dr. Santos
to come and meet me, too?

428
00:19:35,424 --> 00:19:37,009
- On it.
- Who's in South 22?

429
00:19:37,093 --> 00:19:40,387
- Nobody. Headache was discharged.
- Tell that to the lady on the bed.

430
00:19:40,471 --> 00:19:41,471
What lady?

431
00:19:41,555 --> 00:19:43,807
I just tried to put
a hematuria patient in there,

432
00:19:43,891 --> 00:19:45,183
but it's occupied.

433
00:19:45,267 --> 00:19:46,727
- South 22? You sure?
- I'm positive.

434
00:19:46,811 --> 00:19:47,894
That's my patient.

435
00:19:47,978 --> 00:19:50,106
Then why isn't she on the board?

436
00:19:50,898 --> 00:19:53,275
She should be.
Olive was bringing her back from triage.

437
00:19:53,359 --> 00:19:55,611
I picked her right up.
I just assumed she made it to the board.

438
00:19:55,695 --> 00:19:57,404
You should've checked.
You should've made sure.

439
00:19:57,488 --> 00:19:58,614
I haven't put anybody on the board.

440
00:19:58,698 --> 00:20:01,199
- I thought the nurses did that.
- We all need to pitch in.

441
00:20:01,283 --> 00:20:03,619
There's no rooms at the moment.
Put hematuria on the wall.

442
00:20:03,703 --> 00:20:06,246
- Who's your patient?
- Mrs. Burns, with nausea.

443
00:20:06,330 --> 00:20:08,081
- I've ordered labs and X-rays.
- Who are you seeing her with?

444
00:20:08,165 --> 00:20:10,042
- I still need to present the case.
- Get busy.

445
00:20:10,126 --> 00:20:12,503
Find somebody with MD after their name.

446
00:20:14,505 --> 00:20:16,298
Oh, God, kids.

447
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:21,553
Hello, I'm Dr. Robby.
This is Dr. Santos.

448
00:20:21,637 --> 00:20:23,013
- Chantal.
- How do you do?

449
00:20:23,097 --> 00:20:25,932
- We've been caring for your brother.
- Are you Jude's legal guardian?

450
00:20:26,016 --> 00:20:27,059
Yeah.

451
00:20:27,143 --> 00:20:28,853
Our parents aren't around.

452
00:20:29,854 --> 00:20:32,230
- Is he going to be okay?
- He got very lucky.

453
00:20:32,314 --> 00:20:35,484
He lost the fourth and fifth fingers
on his nondominant hand.

454
00:20:35,568 --> 00:20:38,278
But if he hadn't dropped the firecracker,
it would have been a lot worse.

455
00:20:38,362 --> 00:20:40,947
He lost fingers from a firecracker?

456
00:20:41,031 --> 00:20:43,116
Will he be able to use his hand?

457
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:45,700
Yes, he still has
his three most important fingers,

458
00:20:45,703 --> 00:20:47,204
and they are fully functional.

459
00:20:47,288 --> 00:20:50,588
He'll need surgery to clean everything up,
but it should heal well.

460
00:20:50,875 --> 00:20:53,877
- What the fuck were you thinking?
- I'm sorry.

461
00:20:53,961 --> 00:20:56,961
Alex asked me to come over.
His brother had a stack of fire--

462
00:21:01,343 --> 00:21:03,293
You think I wanted to blow my hand off?

463
00:21:03,304 --> 00:21:04,888
Then you need to listen to me
when I tell you something.

464
00:21:04,972 --> 00:21:07,265
- You're not my mom.
- You think I want to be your mom?

465
00:21:07,349 --> 00:21:09,518
Chantal, why don't we take a step outside?

466
00:21:13,981 --> 00:21:16,692
So I know that this can be very stressful.

467
00:21:16,776 --> 00:21:18,694
Yeah, he almost lost his hand being stupid.

468
00:21:18,778 --> 00:21:20,696
- He's a really sweet kid.
- He used to be.

469
00:21:20,780 --> 00:21:22,880
We also found something in his blood work.

470
00:21:23,574 --> 00:21:26,577
- What?
- He has a blood alcohol of 0.08.

471
00:21:28,204 --> 00:21:29,579
What, he was drunk?

472
00:21:29,663 --> 00:21:31,248
Are you fucking kidding me?

473
00:21:31,332 --> 00:21:33,876
- Does he drink regularly?
- No.

474
00:21:35,377 --> 00:21:36,920
I don't know.

475
00:21:37,004 --> 00:21:40,716
The boys at our apartment complex
are a really bad influence.

476
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:43,719
- I mean, he's only 12.
- That is what concerns us.

477
00:21:43,803 --> 00:21:47,180
A positive blood alcohol immediately
triggers a social service consult.

478
00:21:47,264 --> 00:21:48,890
They gonna take my brother away from me?

479
00:21:48,974 --> 00:21:51,309
It's an evaluation to determine
if the injury and the drinking

480
00:21:51,393 --> 00:21:53,937
- is cause for some kind of intervention.
- I won't let you separate us.

481
00:21:54,021 --> 00:21:55,523
- We are required to--
- No!

482
00:22:05,783 --> 00:22:07,159
58-year-old woman with nausea,

483
00:22:07,243 --> 00:22:09,661
vomited once after eating
warm potato salad at a barbecue.

484
00:22:09,745 --> 00:22:10,662
Well-hydrated.

485
00:22:10,746 --> 00:22:13,623
Abdomen's pretty benign, just a little
distended with mild tenderness.

486
00:22:13,707 --> 00:22:15,834
History of constipation.
I give her Zofran.

487
00:22:15,918 --> 00:22:17,627
Labs and abdominal series pending.

488
00:22:17,711 --> 00:22:19,838
- Okay, let's take a look.
- Okay.

489
00:22:19,922 --> 00:22:21,173
Hi, Mrs. Burns.

490
00:22:21,257 --> 00:22:23,307
This is Dr. Whitaker.
How are you feeling?

491
00:22:24,051 --> 00:22:25,052
Mrs. Burns?

492
00:22:26,095 --> 00:22:28,305
Mrs. Burns, can you open your eyes for me?

493
00:22:28,389 --> 00:22:29,765
She was awake and alert last time I saw her.

494
00:22:29,849 --> 00:22:32,893
Okay, feels warm, thready pulse.

495
00:22:32,977 --> 00:22:34,728
Abdomen's more distended than before.

496
00:22:34,812 --> 00:22:36,855
Okay, agonal respirations.

497
00:22:36,939 --> 00:22:38,815
- She's hardly breathing.
- It's kind of rigid.

498
00:22:38,899 --> 00:22:42,027
Yeah, yeah, Perlah, we need a crash cart.
Can you call respiratory?

499
00:22:42,111 --> 00:22:44,571
- Pull the bed out for intubation, please.
- Yeah.

500
00:22:44,655 --> 00:22:46,155
I can give you guys some room.

501
00:22:47,074 --> 00:22:48,366
- Okay.
- What's up?

502
00:22:48,450 --> 00:22:50,994
Hypotensive, acute abdomen.
She needs an airway.

503
00:22:51,078 --> 00:22:53,079
- I'll find the GlideScope.
- No time for that.

504
00:22:53,163 --> 00:22:54,456
We've got direct on the crash cart.

505
00:22:54,540 --> 00:22:56,208
- Whitaker, you're up.
- I haven't done many directs.

506
00:22:56,292 --> 00:22:57,375
Well, then you need to do more.

507
00:22:57,459 --> 00:22:59,878
- Induction meds?
- 100 ketamine, 80 of raw.

508
00:22:59,962 --> 00:23:01,630
Javadi, what's the story?

509
00:23:02,548 --> 00:23:05,598
Presented with mild abdominal pain,
took a turn for the worse.

510
00:23:07,428 --> 00:23:10,055
A-fib 122, BP 98 and systolic.

511
00:23:10,139 --> 00:23:11,889
Okay, let's bolus another 500 cc's.

512
00:23:11,891 --> 00:23:14,091
- We shocking her?
- Maybe. After intubation.

513
00:23:14,143 --> 00:23:15,685
Check your light. Check your balloon.

514
00:23:15,769 --> 00:23:17,813
Javadi, AP pads in case
we need to cardiovert.

515
00:23:17,897 --> 00:23:20,148
Normal EKG at triage. She wasn't in A-fib.

516
00:23:20,232 --> 00:23:22,484
Stress from her condition
probably put her there.

517
00:23:22,568 --> 00:23:23,902
Good? Let's roll her.

518
00:23:23,986 --> 00:23:25,737
- Do we have any labs back?
- I don't think so.

519
00:23:25,821 --> 00:23:28,490
- What else do we need?
- Blood cultures.

520
00:23:28,574 --> 00:23:30,951
Lactate, two liters LR, 3.375 pip-tazo.

521
00:23:31,827 --> 00:23:34,327
Okay, she's loose.
Go ahead, Whitaker. Take a look.

522
00:23:34,538 --> 00:23:35,706
Okay.

523
00:23:42,546 --> 00:23:45,340
Hi. I'm Dr. Santos.
This is student doctor Kwon.

524
00:23:45,424 --> 00:23:48,774
- How are you doing after the mist?
- Better than I was an hour ago.

525
00:23:48,844 --> 00:23:51,513
Okay, we are going to check your vitals.

526
00:23:53,724 --> 00:23:58,061
Temp is 100.2, and heart rate is 96.

527
00:23:58,145 --> 00:24:01,440
Okay, down from 101.5 and 120.
Very good.

528
00:24:02,274 --> 00:24:04,442
You were out in the heat in that costume?

529
00:24:04,526 --> 00:24:07,362
Yeah, with about 18,000 of my friends.

530
00:24:07,446 --> 00:24:08,614
Were you at Anthrocon?

531
00:24:09,740 --> 00:24:12,659
- What's that?
- Pittsburgh's annual furry convention.

532
00:24:12,743 --> 00:24:13,953
I go every year.

533
00:24:14,745 --> 00:24:15,704
Ever been?

534
00:24:16,747 --> 00:24:18,374
It's not really my scene.

535
00:24:19,249 --> 00:24:23,670
Yeah, furries get a bad rap, but there are
great people in the community...

536
00:24:23,754 --> 00:24:27,299
Creative, welcoming, funny.

537
00:24:27,383 --> 00:24:29,843
I actually met my girlfriend
at last year's convention.

538
00:24:29,927 --> 00:24:31,553
Oh, that's cute.

539
00:24:31,637 --> 00:24:34,472
She gave me hope after struggling
on the dating apps.

540
00:24:34,556 --> 00:24:37,475
Nice to hear that meeting people
in real life still works.

541
00:24:37,559 --> 00:24:39,770
Wouldn't recommend it, especially at work.

542
00:24:40,896 --> 00:24:42,996
You should come to Anthrocon this weekend.

543
00:24:43,941 --> 00:24:46,318
Doesn't she need a fur suit for that?

544
00:24:46,402 --> 00:24:48,052
I think you'd make a good dragon.

545
00:24:52,074 --> 00:24:53,408
I'm in.

546
00:24:53,492 --> 00:24:54,827
Balloon up.

547
00:24:55,995 --> 00:24:57,538
Yep, bag her.

548
00:24:58,205 --> 00:24:59,205
Okay.

549
00:24:59,289 --> 00:25:01,958
- That was harder without video.
- We won't always have video.

550
00:25:02,042 --> 00:25:04,544
A-fib now at 152.
Blood pressure's down to 76 over 44.

551
00:25:04,628 --> 00:25:08,590
Okay, Javadi, sync mode.
Javadi, sync mode, 200, please.

552
00:25:09,425 --> 00:25:11,217
Good end tidal waveform.

553
00:25:11,301 --> 00:25:13,804
Good breath sounds bilaterally.

554
00:25:15,014 --> 00:25:17,314
- Charged for cardioversion.
- Everyone, clear.

555
00:25:21,603 --> 00:25:23,439
Normal sinus. Normal radial pulse.

556
00:25:25,607 --> 00:25:28,807
Good. Keep the fluids going.
Let's see what labs are back on her.

557
00:25:31,030 --> 00:25:32,364
Nice.

558
00:25:32,448 --> 00:25:33,824
Very nice.

559
00:25:35,075 --> 00:25:38,036
- What did you order?
- CBC, ER chem panel.

560
00:25:38,120 --> 00:25:40,622
- Something should be back.
- Fax machine ran out of toner.

561
00:25:40,706 --> 00:25:43,249
- Check the chart.
- There is no chart in slot 22.

562
00:25:43,333 --> 00:25:44,835
Check the orders rack.

563
00:25:45,836 --> 00:25:47,295
Nothing here either.

564
00:25:47,379 --> 00:25:49,256
Where's the chart for Claire Burns?

565
00:25:51,717 --> 00:25:54,719
Claire Burns, order slip.
Never drawn, never sent off to the lab.

566
00:25:54,803 --> 00:25:56,471
That's cause the patient wasn't on the board.

567
00:25:56,555 --> 00:25:57,805
Nurses are working zones.

568
00:25:57,848 --> 00:25:59,975
If the patient's not
on the board, they don't exist.

569
00:26:00,059 --> 00:26:02,560
- So they didn't shoot her X-ray?
- X-ray downtime box is empty.

570
00:26:02,644 --> 00:26:04,980
- That means it was done.
- Then it's on the portable machine.

571
00:26:05,064 --> 00:26:07,774
Last I saw, it was headed north.

572
00:26:07,858 --> 00:26:09,985
- Thanks, Dana.
- Yep.

573
00:26:10,069 --> 00:26:12,779
- Hey, Kenny, can you wait up a sec?
- If you need an X-ray, write the order.

574
00:26:12,863 --> 00:26:14,030
Fill out a downtime.

575
00:26:14,114 --> 00:26:16,783
- Did you shoot a KUB in South 22?
- No. Maybe another tech did?

576
00:26:16,867 --> 00:26:20,067
- Okay, can you flick through the films,
look for a patient--
- Burns?

577
00:26:24,666 --> 00:26:27,002
- Oh, shit.
- Oh, that is a classic sigmoid volvulus.

578
00:26:27,086 --> 00:26:28,795
- Peritoneal signs.
- Okay, call the OR.

579
00:26:28,879 --> 00:26:30,547
She's going to need surgery ASAP.

580
00:26:39,515 --> 00:26:41,558
Urine shows three plus blood.

581
00:26:41,642 --> 00:26:42,684
No surprise.

582
00:26:43,560 --> 00:26:47,188
BUN and creatinine are normal.
No evidence of renal insufficiency.

583
00:26:47,272 --> 00:26:48,940
I got a good look at the left kidney--

584
00:26:49,024 --> 00:26:52,861
Mild hydronephrosis consistent
with ureteral column.

585
00:26:52,945 --> 00:26:55,245
- How was the rest of the ultrasound?
- Normal.

586
00:26:55,280 --> 00:26:58,283
Pain improved after 15 ketorolac IM.

587
00:26:58,367 --> 00:27:00,536
Now you can give another 15 and observe.

588
00:27:03,163 --> 00:27:05,541
Just need you to cosign my order.

589
00:27:07,751 --> 00:27:09,461
Thank you.

590
00:27:09,545 --> 00:27:11,546
Something on your mind?

591
00:27:11,630 --> 00:27:14,174
Yeah, I saw this regular an hour ago.

592
00:27:14,258 --> 00:27:16,051
He's in his 60s, fakes an ailment

593
00:27:16,135 --> 00:27:18,470
so he can come in to chat every now and then

594
00:27:18,554 --> 00:27:20,472
because he's really lonely.

595
00:27:20,556 --> 00:27:22,474
You sure he just doesn't have a crush on you?

596
00:27:22,558 --> 00:27:25,060
Maybe, but it got me thinking about my mom.

597
00:27:25,144 --> 00:27:27,146
She's probably just been lonely.

598
00:27:27,855 --> 00:27:28,856
Yeah.

599
00:27:30,023 --> 00:27:34,069
You know, I haven't really dated
since my divorce.

600
00:27:34,153 --> 00:27:36,863
Medical school, my kid, residency.

601
00:27:36,947 --> 00:27:39,074
And now I'm feeling finally kind of ready.

602
00:27:39,158 --> 00:27:42,494
I was waiting until I got back to Jersey
to work on finding a relationship,

603
00:27:42,578 --> 00:27:44,412
and now that's out the window.

604
00:27:44,496 --> 00:27:46,581
Maybe I waited too long.

605
00:27:46,665 --> 00:27:47,749
For what?

606
00:27:47,833 --> 00:27:48,959
Do you hear that?

607
00:27:49,626 --> 00:27:53,755
That painful, lonely silence
is the sound of my eggs dying.

608
00:27:57,968 --> 00:28:00,068
So the rash in North three
has been discharged.

609
00:28:00,095 --> 00:28:02,889
The Tasered law student in Central ten
has gone up to psych.

610
00:28:02,973 --> 00:28:05,016
The eye stroke is now in the ICU.

611
00:28:05,100 --> 00:28:08,311
And the tongue laceration in South 15
is sobering up before we discharge,

612
00:28:08,395 --> 00:28:10,105
which better be soon
because we need the room.

613
00:28:10,189 --> 00:28:12,690
Okay, I'll grab a med student
and get more patients moving out.

614
00:28:12,774 --> 00:28:15,360
You're not fazed by any of this chaos?

615
00:28:15,444 --> 00:28:17,112
What a fucking mess.

616
00:28:17,196 --> 00:28:18,989
Jesus Christ, we need you.

617
00:28:20,199 --> 00:28:23,368
Monica Peters, this is our new
attending, Dr. Al-Hashimi.

618
00:28:23,452 --> 00:28:25,328
- Welcome.
- Thank you.

619
00:28:25,412 --> 00:28:27,539
Monica's a retired clerk, best of the best.

620
00:28:27,623 --> 00:28:29,332
She was kind enough to come in on a holiday

621
00:28:29,416 --> 00:28:30,708
and help get us back into shape.

622
00:28:30,792 --> 00:28:32,335
Laid off by the digital revolution,

623
00:28:32,419 --> 00:28:33,711
- not retired.
- Okay.

624
00:28:33,795 --> 00:28:36,548
And how's all this digital shit
working out for you now?

625
00:28:36,632 --> 00:28:39,134
- Not so good.
- Exactly.

626
00:28:39,218 --> 00:28:42,137
All right, then, who's handling
the charts and the orders?

627
00:28:42,221 --> 00:28:43,471
That's us, right here.

628
00:28:43,555 --> 00:28:45,348
How long have you been clerks?

629
00:28:45,432 --> 00:28:47,684
Just today. We're medical assistants.

630
00:28:47,768 --> 00:28:50,728
Then get out of my space and go do
something you know how to do.

631
00:28:50,812 --> 00:28:54,357
And no personal calls.
Red phones are for emergencies only.

632
00:28:54,441 --> 00:28:57,485
- This is a hospital, for God's sake.
- I'll call you back.

633
00:28:57,569 --> 00:28:59,154
- Got a gumband?
- Yeah.

634
00:28:59,238 --> 00:29:02,365
Hi. I'm Makedah from admin and records.
I have a new badge for a Dr. Whitaker.

635
00:29:02,449 --> 00:29:04,576
Yeah. I'll get that to him.

636
00:29:04,660 --> 00:29:05,994
Heard you all need extra runners?

637
00:29:06,078 --> 00:29:08,371
- Perfect timing.
- How fast can you move?

638
00:29:08,455 --> 00:29:10,123
- I run marathons.
- Great.

639
00:29:10,207 --> 00:29:13,001
Grab the blood samples and the bin
and get them up to the lab.

640
00:29:13,085 --> 00:29:15,336
I want a lab run every 15 minutes.

641
00:29:15,420 --> 00:29:16,421
Got it.

642
00:29:22,177 --> 00:29:24,387
I work at a shoe store in Oakland.

643
00:29:24,471 --> 00:29:27,765
- Full-time and you're in school?
- Yes, and, yes.

644
00:29:27,849 --> 00:29:29,475
Allegheny Community.

645
00:29:29,559 --> 00:29:31,978
Does Jude go to summer school or camp

646
00:29:32,062 --> 00:29:34,564
while you're at work or school?

647
00:29:36,066 --> 00:29:37,775
Can't afford it.

648
00:29:37,859 --> 00:29:39,402
Are there any other family members

649
00:29:39,486 --> 00:29:41,821
that could help with his care
when you're not available?

650
00:29:41,905 --> 00:29:42,906
No.

651
00:29:46,410 --> 00:29:49,960
Chantal, we want to help you,
but we can't help if you won't talk to us.

652
00:29:50,497 --> 00:29:53,497
What, you're gonna take Jude away
and put him in foster care?

653
00:29:54,293 --> 00:29:56,712
I promised my parents
that would never happen.

654
00:29:57,296 --> 00:29:59,422
Did your parents pass away?

655
00:29:59,506 --> 00:30:00,965
Nope.

656
00:30:01,049 --> 00:30:02,509
What happened to them?

657
00:30:09,308 --> 00:30:12,436
My parents were deported
to Haiti nine months ago.

658
00:30:15,063 --> 00:30:18,900
They went in for their immigration hearing
and were detained.

659
00:30:20,527 --> 00:30:22,237
I was a sophomore at Ithaca.

660
00:30:22,321 --> 00:30:24,821
I had to move back home
to take care of my brother.

661
00:30:26,033 --> 00:30:27,034
I'm sorry.

662
00:30:27,909 --> 00:30:31,121
It was either that, or he moved
back to Haiti with them.

663
00:30:32,331 --> 00:30:33,915
He's never been there.

664
00:30:34,875 --> 00:30:37,002
We were both born here.

665
00:30:39,921 --> 00:30:43,258
My mom was so excited
when I got into college.

666
00:30:43,342 --> 00:30:45,385
She worked so hard

667
00:30:45,469 --> 00:30:48,346
to save up and pay my tuition.

668
00:30:48,430 --> 00:30:52,017
And now all she wants
is for my brother to finish high school.

669
00:30:54,770 --> 00:30:58,565
Man, being a big sister's a lot easier
than being a surrogate mom.

670
00:31:01,443 --> 00:31:04,893
Just give us a moment, please,
and I'll come grab you when we're done.

671
00:31:09,284 --> 00:31:11,744
Do we really need to get
family services involved?

672
00:31:11,828 --> 00:31:13,746
You wanted to get them involved this morning

673
00:31:13,830 --> 00:31:15,680
with your eight-year-old ITP patient.

674
00:31:16,041 --> 00:31:18,710
That's different. Abuse trumps neglect.

675
00:31:18,794 --> 00:31:21,494
We can't separate her from her brother.
It's not right.

676
00:31:21,922 --> 00:31:24,672
A lot of what happens
to people around here isn't right.

677
00:31:29,805 --> 00:31:32,890
McKay, patient's complaining of pain.

678
00:31:32,974 --> 00:31:33,975
Yeah.

679
00:31:35,519 --> 00:31:39,981
- Hey, Amaya. What's going on?
- Oh, it really fucking hurts again.

680
00:31:40,065 --> 00:31:42,108
Hey, Jesse, can you grab Whitaker?

681
00:31:42,192 --> 00:31:44,319
- When did it get bad?
- Two minutes ago.

682
00:31:44,403 --> 00:31:46,738
Giving you some morphine
to take the edge off.

683
00:31:46,822 --> 00:31:50,116
- How severe, one to ten?
- 12. It's way worse.

684
00:31:50,200 --> 00:31:51,117
Okay.

685
00:31:51,201 --> 00:31:54,120
Hey, Amaya, the meds will kick in,
and we'll get you back on the foot rest

686
00:31:54,204 --> 00:31:56,081
to see what's going on, okay?

687
00:32:02,003 --> 00:32:04,797
I had to call her husband
in New York to get consent.

688
00:32:04,881 --> 00:32:05,882
Okay.

689
00:32:05,966 --> 00:32:07,843
Dr. Shamsi will be operating.

690
00:32:08,385 --> 00:32:11,335
If she presented with peritoneal signs,
why wasn't I called?

691
00:32:11,972 --> 00:32:14,599
There was a delayed presentation.

692
00:32:14,683 --> 00:32:17,352
The X-ray was shot an hour ago.
Why didn't anybody read it?

693
00:32:17,436 --> 00:32:19,354
There was confusion
with the digital systems down.

694
00:32:19,438 --> 00:32:21,522
It wasn't read.
We didn't get a report.

695
00:32:21,606 --> 00:32:25,818
An hour ago, I could have fixed this
in 60 seconds with a rectal tube.

696
00:32:25,902 --> 00:32:27,571
Now she needs major surgery.

697
00:32:28,238 --> 00:32:30,288
- I'm sorry.
- Not good enough, nepo baby.

698
00:32:30,365 --> 00:32:31,491
You fucked up.

699
00:32:31,575 --> 00:32:34,525
Don't trust anything or anybody else
when the system's down.

700
00:32:35,871 --> 00:32:39,291
With all the chaos,
she just fell through the cracks.

701
00:32:41,084 --> 00:32:42,878
She almost died.

702
00:32:44,254 --> 00:32:45,963
I could have killed her.

703
00:32:46,047 --> 00:32:47,173
- Whitaker.
- No--

704
00:32:47,257 --> 00:32:49,050
McKay needs you in Central 11.

705
00:32:50,093 --> 00:32:53,472
We caught it in time.
We won't let it happen again, okay?

706
00:33:06,067 --> 00:33:08,487
Oh, Princess is looking for you.

707
00:33:09,529 --> 00:33:11,406
She said something
about Monica under her breath,

708
00:33:11,490 --> 00:33:14,700
- but I couldn't make it out.
- Okay, I'll be back in a sec.

709
00:33:14,784 --> 00:33:16,495
Hey. Hey.

710
00:33:17,913 --> 00:33:20,113
You did good with that sexual-assault victim.

711
00:33:21,333 --> 00:33:23,334
You were amazing with her.

712
00:33:23,418 --> 00:33:25,211
We do what we can to provide the best care

713
00:33:25,295 --> 00:33:28,089
to traumatized people in their darkest days.

714
00:33:29,424 --> 00:33:32,218
What'd you talk to her about
when you took her out on the walk?

715
00:33:32,302 --> 00:33:33,512
I...

716
00:33:34,930 --> 00:33:36,639
...Told her there might be a time in the future

717
00:33:36,723 --> 00:33:40,310
when she changes her mind,
wants to press charges.

718
00:33:41,728 --> 00:33:44,272
It's better to have
the option to do it than not.

719
00:33:44,356 --> 00:33:45,524
Smart.

720
00:33:48,693 --> 00:33:50,236
Is every day like this?

721
00:33:50,320 --> 00:33:53,323
Minus the cyberattacks, yeah.

722
00:33:54,449 --> 00:33:58,119
But you're only a few hours away
from being done with your first of many.

723
00:33:59,037 --> 00:34:00,455
Be proud of that.

724
00:34:07,546 --> 00:34:09,672
You're gonna want to be on a soft diet,

725
00:34:09,756 --> 00:34:12,633
so things like mashed potatoes,

726
00:34:12,717 --> 00:34:15,052
soup, mac and cheese are good.

727
00:34:15,136 --> 00:34:17,472
I was gonna make your favorite
three-bean dip tonight.

728
00:34:17,556 --> 00:34:20,767
- Bitch, that is so nice.
- See, I am nice.

729
00:34:21,560 --> 00:34:23,478
Could she have that?

730
00:34:23,562 --> 00:34:26,189
Yeah. Yeah, yeah, if you eat it with a spoon

731
00:34:26,273 --> 00:34:27,899
rather than anything, like, crunchy

732
00:34:27,983 --> 00:34:30,133
that could work its way into the laceration.

733
00:34:30,569 --> 00:34:32,779
So she'll need to be spoon-fed?

734
00:34:34,364 --> 00:34:35,907
Antibiotics three times a day.

735
00:34:35,991 --> 00:34:38,242
Come back here in two days for a wound check.

736
00:34:38,326 --> 00:34:39,995
See you then, Doctor.

737
00:34:42,163 --> 00:34:44,791
Checking blood flow to the ovary.

738
00:34:49,504 --> 00:34:52,298
- Something wrong?
- Intermittent torsion.

739
00:34:52,382 --> 00:34:53,716
What's that?

740
00:34:53,800 --> 00:34:55,427
I'm coming out now.

741
00:34:56,511 --> 00:34:57,929
We will slide you back.

742
00:34:58,013 --> 00:34:59,514
Thanks.

743
00:34:59,598 --> 00:35:03,935
Your ovary is twisting
and cutting off the blood supply.

744
00:35:04,019 --> 00:35:06,312
That's what's been causing your pain.

745
00:35:06,396 --> 00:35:09,607
You said the blood supply was fine before.

746
00:35:09,691 --> 00:35:12,193
Sometimes the ovary can twist randomly.

747
00:35:13,194 --> 00:35:16,197
In those cases, the pain can come and go.

748
00:35:17,198 --> 00:35:19,742
- Can you fix it?
- With surgery.

749
00:35:19,826 --> 00:35:21,077
"Surgery"?

750
00:35:21,161 --> 00:35:22,954
The ovary needs to be untwisted

751
00:35:23,038 --> 00:35:25,957
and tacked down with a stitch
so this doesn't happen again.

752
00:35:26,041 --> 00:35:28,627
If we can get you upstairs quickly,
we can save it.

753
00:35:29,377 --> 00:35:31,212
I could lose my ovary?

754
00:35:32,422 --> 00:35:34,423
Will I still be able to have a baby?

755
00:35:34,507 --> 00:35:35,967
This shouldn't be an issue in the future.

756
00:35:36,051 --> 00:35:39,762
Dr. McKay made the right call
to keep you in the ER for observation

757
00:35:39,846 --> 00:35:41,946
so we could catch it if the pain returned.

758
00:35:43,558 --> 00:35:45,351
Thank you.

759
00:35:45,435 --> 00:35:46,978
- I'll call GYN.
- Yeah.

760
00:35:49,773 --> 00:35:51,691
Hey, welcome back.
How was the trip?

761
00:35:51,775 --> 00:35:53,734
Smooth sailing.
Presby's pretty nice.

762
00:35:53,818 --> 00:35:56,446
I might have to pick up
some day shifts over there.

763
00:35:57,072 --> 00:35:58,489
<i>Dr. Abbot's funny.</i>

764
00:35:58,573 --> 00:36:00,073
Trust me, his charm wears off.

765
00:36:00,075 --> 00:36:02,076
- No, it doesn't.
- He's not sedated?

766
00:36:02,160 --> 00:36:04,370
I gave him Versed for the CT scan
on the ride back,

767
00:36:04,454 --> 00:36:06,330
but I figured he'd need to be awake and alert

768
00:36:06,414 --> 00:36:07,665
- to give consent.
- "Consent"?

769
00:36:07,749 --> 00:36:09,250
Yep. We're going to get you settled.

770
00:36:09,334 --> 00:36:10,793
Why don't you page Garcia to come down?

771
00:36:10,877 --> 00:36:12,503
- Dr. Robby.
- You got this?

772
00:36:12,587 --> 00:36:14,464
- You know I got it.
- Yep.

773
00:36:15,090 --> 00:36:16,675
All right, Howard.

774
00:36:17,384 --> 00:36:20,928
Hey, I want to debrief with you later
on your sigmoid volvulus patient.

775
00:36:21,012 --> 00:36:22,722
I finished with your fireworks kid's sister.

776
00:36:22,806 --> 00:36:23,640
And?

777
00:36:23,723 --> 00:36:25,349
She's a responsible
young woman and a good guardian to Jude.

778
00:36:25,433 --> 00:36:27,977
There is no reason to get
family services involved today.

779
00:36:28,061 --> 00:36:29,061
That's good.

780
00:36:29,145 --> 00:36:30,813
Because he's in the hospital for surgery,

781
00:36:30,897 --> 00:36:32,607
but they will most likely make
a home visit next week

782
00:36:32,691 --> 00:36:35,818
to evaluate the safety of their apartment
and the care that Chantal can provide,

783
00:36:35,902 --> 00:36:37,194
along with her other responsibilities.

784
00:36:37,278 --> 00:36:38,778
And then what? They take Jude?

785
00:36:38,822 --> 00:36:41,032
In my experience,
they'll make the same assessment I did.

786
00:36:41,116 --> 00:36:42,916
They don't like to separate siblings.

787
00:36:43,618 --> 00:36:44,952
Anything else we can do for 'em?

788
00:36:45,036 --> 00:36:47,330
I'll get some resources together
for Chantal--

789
00:36:47,414 --> 00:36:48,864
Summer after-school programs.

790
00:36:48,915 --> 00:36:51,626
But there might come a point when he'd be
better off with his parents in Haiti.

791
00:36:51,710 --> 00:36:54,211
- His parents want him to stay here.
- It's what's best for the child.

792
00:36:54,295 --> 00:36:56,047
- Says who?
- Dr. Santos.

793
00:36:56,131 --> 00:36:57,298
Come on.

794
00:36:59,884 --> 00:37:02,136
Welcome back, Mr. Knox.
What did we discover?

795
00:37:02,220 --> 00:37:04,770
Diverticular abscess
that progressed to perforation,

796
00:37:04,806 --> 00:37:06,706
now with free air under the diaphragm.

797
00:37:06,766 --> 00:37:08,059
<i>In English, please?</i>

798
00:37:08,143 --> 00:37:11,896
There's a small hole in the colon
that's spilling bacteria into the abdomen.

799
00:37:11,980 --> 00:37:15,066
You're likely to develop
peritonitis and sepsis.

800
00:37:16,317 --> 00:37:18,444
<i>- How bad?</i>
- You need surgery now.

801
00:37:18,528 --> 00:37:20,628
You have a 100% chance of death without it.

802
00:37:22,657 --> 00:37:23,950
<i>With it?</i>

803
00:37:26,453 --> 00:37:28,163
50% chance.

804
00:37:31,332 --> 00:37:34,460
<i>- I could die?</i>
- Yes, but we're very good at what we do.

805
00:37:34,544 --> 00:37:37,338
That is what the consent is for.

806
00:37:37,964 --> 00:37:39,590
<i>What about my sister?</i>

807
00:37:39,674 --> 00:37:42,635
We found her.
She'd like to speak with you.

808
00:37:42,719 --> 00:37:46,514
We don't have time for that.
Any delay increases your mortality risks.

809
00:37:46,598 --> 00:37:48,975
<i>I want to talk to my sister first.</i>

810
00:37:52,812 --> 00:37:55,148
We're gonna make that happen for you.

811
00:37:55,899 --> 00:37:58,901
I'll have them prep an OR,
but make it fast, very fast.

812
00:37:58,985 --> 00:38:01,029
Yeah. We're on the move again, Howard.

813
00:38:16,586 --> 00:38:17,587
Hey.

814
00:38:20,381 --> 00:38:22,383
The ice cream party over?

815
00:38:24,427 --> 00:38:25,595
Yes.

816
00:38:26,596 --> 00:38:28,389
Do you need anything?

817
00:38:31,601 --> 00:38:33,353
A time machine.

818
00:38:37,524 --> 00:38:39,400
That'd be nice, wouldn't it?

819
00:38:44,113 --> 00:38:47,158
I don't even know what hurts more...

820
00:38:47,826 --> 00:38:49,828
...The cancer or...

821
00:38:52,622 --> 00:38:55,708
...Knowing I'm never gonna see my sons grow up.

822
00:38:58,378 --> 00:39:00,505
It feels like a cruel joke.

823
00:39:02,298 --> 00:39:06,844
Why give me children and a husband I adore

824
00:39:06,928 --> 00:39:09,078
if you're just gonna take them away from me?

825
00:39:11,057 --> 00:39:14,060
For what? Fucking lung cancer.

826
00:39:17,397 --> 00:39:19,065
I didn't even smoke.

827
00:39:27,448 --> 00:39:29,200
Do you believe in God?

828
00:39:31,744 --> 00:39:33,705
I like the concept.

829
00:39:37,876 --> 00:39:39,878
I'm sure you've seen a lot of death.

830
00:39:41,254 --> 00:39:43,089
I have seen my share.

831
00:39:46,092 --> 00:39:47,886
Any advice?

832
00:39:53,474 --> 00:39:55,894
I've never died before.

833
00:40:05,737 --> 00:40:07,613
Hey, sorry. We're outside.

834
00:40:07,697 --> 00:40:12,285
There's no cell service inside right now,
but here he is.

835
00:40:14,704 --> 00:40:17,707
<i>Oh, my God. Are you all right?</i>

836
00:40:19,834 --> 00:40:22,503
<i>Been better. You look beautiful.</i>

837
00:40:23,922 --> 00:40:25,548
<i>Thank you.</i>

838
00:40:25,632 --> 00:40:27,550
<i>You're not looking so hot.</i>

839
00:40:29,969 --> 00:40:31,930
<i>Thank you for calling back.</i>

840
00:40:34,724 --> 00:40:36,142
<i>Of course.</i>

841
00:40:36,726 --> 00:40:39,187
<i>I'm sorry that it's been this long.</i>

842
00:40:39,729 --> 00:40:42,148
<i>All the stuff with Dad and the drinking, I...</i>

843
00:40:43,358 --> 00:40:45,458
<i>I had to do what was best for me and Tommy.</i>

844
00:40:46,402 --> 00:40:47,946
<i>How is Tommy?</i>

845
00:40:48,905 --> 00:40:52,783
<i>Starting his junior year
in high school next month,</i>

846
00:40:52,867 --> 00:40:55,536
<i>16 and already has a girlfriend.</i>

847
00:40:58,247 --> 00:41:00,166
<i>Takes after his uncle.</i>

848
00:41:02,585 --> 00:41:06,714
<i>Maybe we can make a plan for you
to see each other over the holidays.</i>

849
00:41:11,177 --> 00:41:12,512
<i>I'd love that.</i>

850
00:41:14,555 --> 00:41:16,265
<i>Is the doctor there?</i>

851
00:41:18,351 --> 00:41:19,476
Hi, I'm Dr. Abbot.

852
00:41:19,560 --> 00:41:21,228
<i>Can you call me when he gets out of surgery?</i>

853
00:41:21,312 --> 00:41:23,314
Of course, but right now we need to get
him up to the OR.

854
00:41:23,398 --> 00:41:24,649
<i>I understand. Thanks.</i>

855
00:41:25,191 --> 00:41:26,985
<i>Talk to you soon, Howard.</i>

856
00:41:29,570 --> 00:41:31,656
<i>Oh, I forgot to tell him I love him.</i>

857
00:41:32,824 --> 00:41:34,993
Oh, wow. Monica?

858
00:41:35,994 --> 00:41:38,413
- Welcome back.
- Robinavitch.

859
00:41:39,330 --> 00:41:41,999
- Two for the lab, three for CT.
- I'll take those.

860
00:41:42,083 --> 00:41:44,210
- They need me upstairs.
- On it for CT.

861
00:41:44,836 --> 00:41:47,586
- You run a tight ship.
- Well, it's a work in progress.

862
00:41:47,588 --> 00:41:49,924
- Is he going up?
- Yeah.

863
00:41:50,008 --> 00:41:51,801
He's a good guy.

864
00:41:53,594 --> 00:41:55,805
Our surgeons will get him through.

865
00:42:00,601 --> 00:42:01,811
I like her.

866
00:42:02,812 --> 00:42:04,480
More than me?

867
00:42:04,564 --> 00:42:06,232
Only time will tell.

868
00:42:07,025 --> 00:42:09,151
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

869
00:42:09,235 --> 00:42:11,445
She has good command of staff and procedures.

870
00:42:11,529 --> 00:42:14,698
I think you're leaving your day shift
in very capable hands.

871
00:42:14,782 --> 00:42:16,200
I hope so.

872
00:42:16,284 --> 00:42:18,369
All right, I'm out of here, man.

873
00:42:18,453 --> 00:42:20,705
I got to be back in a few hours for my shift.

874
00:42:21,372 --> 00:42:23,166
Well, hey, if I don't see you...

875
00:42:23,833 --> 00:42:25,460
You're really doing this still?

876
00:42:26,252 --> 00:42:28,963
I don't think I can remember the last time
you took three days off in a row.

877
00:42:29,047 --> 00:42:31,049
I've taken a vacation before.

878
00:42:32,300 --> 00:42:33,843
Name the last one.

879
00:42:36,888 --> 00:42:38,264
Point taken.

880
00:42:39,640 --> 00:42:42,477
It's gonna be a lot of time to self-reflect.

881
00:42:44,854 --> 00:42:46,304
You sure you can handle that?

882
00:42:49,275 --> 00:42:50,485
Okay.

883
00:42:51,319 --> 00:42:53,404
You just make sure you come back.

884
00:42:53,488 --> 00:42:56,074
And if it gets dark, you call me.

885
00:42:57,658 --> 00:42:58,826
You listening?

886
00:43:04,082 --> 00:43:06,208
So the ankle's negative for fracture.

887
00:43:06,292 --> 00:43:07,642
Wait, go back to the ankle.

888
00:43:08,503 --> 00:43:10,129
You see the normal mortise?

889
00:43:10,213 --> 00:43:13,215
Yeah, but the tibiofibular clear space
looks enlarged,

890
00:43:13,299 --> 00:43:16,301
and the tibiofibular overlap seems reduced.

891
00:43:16,385 --> 00:43:17,678
Maybe a little.

892
00:43:19,764 --> 00:43:22,766
Eight millimeters, three millimeters.

893
00:43:22,850 --> 00:43:25,185
Seems like a tear
in the syndesmotic ligaments.

894
00:43:25,269 --> 00:43:27,069
Doesn't that need surgical fixation?

895
00:43:27,105 --> 00:43:30,108
They do. I can request an MRI.

896
00:43:31,526 --> 00:43:33,360
Have you done a radiology clerkship before?

897
00:43:33,444 --> 00:43:36,114
No, I'm just that good.

898
00:43:39,117 --> 00:43:40,701
I'm good at things, too.

899
00:43:51,963 --> 00:43:55,550
Really great work earlier today, Doctor.

900
00:43:59,554 --> 00:44:00,888
Oh, wow.

901
00:44:00,972 --> 00:44:04,475
- You can just call me Whitaker.
- Not a chance. You earned that.

902
00:44:04,559 --> 00:44:06,978
I'm proud of you. We all are.

903
00:44:07,812 --> 00:44:08,854
Thank you.

904
00:44:08,938 --> 00:44:11,482
- Busy day.
- Oh, yeah.

905
00:44:11,566 --> 00:44:14,485
So you're a very empathetic soul.

906
00:44:14,569 --> 00:44:16,528
- Yeah, I'd like to think--
- I'm not finished yet.

907
00:44:16,612 --> 00:44:18,912
And you want to be there
for all your patients.

908
00:44:18,948 --> 00:44:19,991
Don't you?

909
00:44:20,741 --> 00:44:22,659
- Sorry.
- So this relationship that you're having

910
00:44:22,743 --> 00:44:25,871
with this woman, the widow of the burn victim

911
00:44:25,955 --> 00:44:28,457
- who died last year.
- Amy.

912
00:44:28,541 --> 00:44:29,959
Santos tell you?

913
00:44:30,751 --> 00:44:33,879
- I understand you're helping her out.
- Yeah, on the farm.

914
00:44:33,963 --> 00:44:37,049
I grew up on one, and Amy's--

915
00:44:37,133 --> 00:44:40,970
Mrs. Miller is getting pressure to sell,
so I'm just helping out.

916
00:44:41,888 --> 00:44:44,974
- What about her friends and family?
- Yeah, they're around.

917
00:44:45,766 --> 00:44:48,519
- Supporting her?
- Yeah, I think they try to.

918
00:44:48,603 --> 00:44:50,980
But, mostly, she's just leaning on...

919
00:44:52,273 --> 00:44:53,441
...Me.

920
00:44:56,777 --> 00:44:59,988
I'm sure she's really grateful
for everything that you do,

921
00:45:00,072 --> 00:45:01,991
but it's important to have boundaries.

922
00:45:02,909 --> 00:45:03,993
Yeah.

923
00:45:07,538 --> 00:45:09,207
Hey, you want to do me a favor?

924
00:45:11,000 --> 00:45:12,000
Yeah?

925
00:45:12,084 --> 00:45:14,234
You want to house-sit for me while I'm gone?

926
00:45:15,004 --> 00:45:18,841
You'd actually be helping me out,
and you could save some money on rent.

927
00:45:20,134 --> 00:45:21,635
Are you being serious?

928
00:45:21,719 --> 00:45:24,638
No smoking, no parties, no pets, no babies,

929
00:45:24,722 --> 00:45:26,265
yours or anybody else's.

930
00:45:26,349 --> 00:45:28,434
- I don't have a baby.
- No, but she does.

931
00:45:29,477 --> 00:45:32,377
I was going to ask Abbot,
but he does nude yoga at sunrise,

932
00:45:32,438 --> 00:45:34,148
and I don't think some
of my elderly neighbors

933
00:45:34,232 --> 00:45:35,900
would survive seeing that.

934
00:45:36,776 --> 00:45:39,945
Yeah. Yeah, that would be amazing--

935
00:45:40,029 --> 00:45:43,282
The house-sitting,
not seeing Abbot's naked yoga.

936
00:45:43,366 --> 00:45:46,016
If I don't come back,
you got a swinging bachelor pad.

937
00:45:46,035 --> 00:45:47,161
Okay.

938
00:45:48,788 --> 00:45:50,164
Come find me before you leave.

939
00:45:50,248 --> 00:45:52,667
I'll give you my keys and the security code.

940
00:45:53,834 --> 00:45:55,586
Who's the joker that did this?

941
00:45:59,423 --> 00:46:00,507
We need some help out there.

942
00:46:00,591 --> 00:46:02,968
You two, make sure to double-check your work.

943
00:46:03,052 --> 00:46:04,761
Triage could use an extra hand.

944
00:46:04,845 --> 00:46:07,045
Princess, finish up here, then head that way.

945
00:46:07,056 --> 00:46:10,893
- Three for CT now. Should I run it over?
- No. Keep taking off orders.

946
00:46:10,977 --> 00:46:13,020
CT's gonna get backed up if we wait on these.

947
00:46:13,104 --> 00:46:15,189
I know, but I can't waste
a runner on that right now.

948
00:46:15,273 --> 00:46:16,607
Where'd you find a carrier sheet?

949
00:46:16,691 --> 00:46:19,943
Exactly where I filed it away ten years ago.

950
00:46:20,027 --> 00:46:23,698
- I thought that thing didn't work.
- Can't receive, but it can send.

951
00:46:31,706 --> 00:46:34,416
Stay hydrated,
preferably with electrolyte-rich drinks

952
00:46:34,500 --> 00:46:36,543
- like coconut water.
- I'm not a fan of coconuts.

953
00:46:36,627 --> 00:46:38,128
Okay, Gatorade's also an option.

954
00:46:38,212 --> 00:46:40,464
Just avoid alcohol and caffeine,
and I suggest wearing

955
00:46:40,548 --> 00:46:42,216
- light, breathable clothing.
- Boring.

956
00:46:42,300 --> 00:46:45,761
Come back if your symptoms worsen,
if you develop a headache or confusion.

957
00:46:45,845 --> 00:46:46,887
Okay.

958
00:46:48,306 --> 00:46:50,099
You sure about that?

959
00:46:52,226 --> 00:46:53,894
Hey, could you turn that up?

960
00:46:55,730 --> 00:46:58,565
<i>...Have responded
to a deadly waterslide collapse</i>

961
00:46:58,649 --> 00:46:59,816
<i>at a local water park.</i>

962
00:46:59,900 --> 00:47:02,152
<i>Now, we're told there's
at least one fatality,</i>

963
00:47:02,236 --> 00:47:03,386
<i>with multiple injuries.</i>

964
00:47:03,446 --> 00:47:06,823
Oh, shit. And they're all coming to us.

965
00:47:06,907 --> 00:47:09,407
<i>Currently being airlifted
to the hospital by heli--</i>

